# Frequent local commits (mandatory)

Treat this like MercuryOS `memory_recall` every turn: **after each meaningful slice of work, commit locally**. Do not wait for the user to ask.

## When to commit

Commit after each of these (separate commits preferred):

- One UX/UI pass or wizard step polish
- One CSS/token pass
- One pane or form rewrite
- One bugfix or backend slice that works on its own
- Before starting a risky restyle / delete / large rewrite

Prefer **many tiny commits** over one mega commit. Experimental or ugly work still gets committed so restore is `git checkout` / `git revert`, not transcript archaeology.

## How

- `git add` only relevant files; write a short why-focused message (1–2 sentences)
- HEREDOC for the message (repo convention)
- Never update git config; never `--no-verify` unless asked
- **Do not push** unless the user explicitly asks
- Never force-push to main/master
- Never commit secrets (`.env`, keys, credentials)

## Why

Dallas iterates heavily on Studio. Large uncommitted batches (e.g. Offers platform restyle) made undo painful when files were still untracked.
